#: ../../../developer/releases/1_0/release-notes.rst:44
#: a7e225577e284622b5aaef3b18171c62
msgid "Upgrading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/1_0/release-notes.rst:48
#: 99f62ee4d8504bae909307d3eab9ae91
msgid "From Qubes 1.0-rc1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/1_0/release-notes.rst:51
#: d7139ca2db45420faf45a6f4e0e2d4b8
msgid ""
"If you’re already running Qubes 1.0-rc1, you don’t need to reinstall, it’s "
"just enough to update the packages in your Dom0 and the template VM(s). The "
"easiest way for doing this is to click on the Update Button in the Qubes "
"Manger – one click when you selected Dom0, and one click for each of your "
"template VM (by default there is just one template)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/1_0/release-notes.rst:54
#: e4232697f1404da8a564497bc187248a
msgid "From Qubes 1.0 Beta 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/releases/1_0/release-notes.rst:57
#: e332ebf3732a4df49c502436843b4e3b
msgid ""
"If you have Qubes Beta 3 currently installed on your system, you must "
"reinstall from scratch, as we offer no direct upgrade option in the "
"installer (sorry). However, we do offer tools for smooth migration of your "
"AppVMs. In order to do that, please backup your AppVMs using the ``qvm-"
"backup`` tool :doc:`as usual </user/how-to-guides/how-to-back-up-restore-and-"
"migrate>`. Then, after you install Qubes 1.0 rc1, you can restore them using "
"``qvm-backup-restore`` tool. However, because we have changed the default "
"template in RC1, you should tell qvm-back-restore about that by passing ``--"
"replace-template`` option:"
msgstr ""
